  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 102.27 Bulky waste",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 102.27 “Bulky waste” means large items that cannot be handled by normal solid waste processing, collection, or disposal methods, such as white goods, furniture, large auto parts, tires, and, when they are not buried on-site in accordance with RSA 149-M:4, XXII, tree stumps.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 102.23) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
